# mesa-iceland: Mesa for the OnePlus Pad 4 (Adreno 840) = the tree of our Fedora build
# 26.3.1^git20261120.6cd33b7-1.fc45.iceland1:
#  - source: mesa-26.3.1-git20261120.6cd33b7.tar.xz = `git archive` of mesa staging/26.3 commit
#    6cd33b7f68ee04c5270215591b2d29535af291bd (tree 51fe67c7...), the same file as in the Fedora SRPM; makepkg does no
#    network fetch for it (SOURCES-NOT-STAGED.txt has its size and sha256);
#  - patches 9101-9142 (this directory) (A840 turnip / ir3 / freedreno MRs + armada 0016 / 0017), applied in the
#    spec's order; venus-protocol v1.1.3 unpacked into subprojects (as the spec's %prep);
#  - meson options from the Fedora spec where they apply (platforms x11,wayland; freedreno-kmds msm,virtio;
#    gallium-va; gles1 / gles2; gbm; glx=dri; egl; glvnd; shared LLVM; valgrind; libunwind; lmsensors; spirv-tools;
#    vulkan-layers device-select; rusticl ON because the Fedora build enables it (with_opencl) -> opencl-mesa-iceland),
#    with the driver lists CUT to what the tablet uses:
#      gallium: freedreno, zink, llvmpipe, softpipe, virgl     vulkan: freedreno (turnip), swrast (lavapipe), virtio
#    (no teflon / NPU, no nouveau / NVK, so no NVK crates); b_ndebug=true as Arch.
# Not Arch's 17-way split: mesa-iceland (GL / EGL / GLES / GBM / DRI / VA / device-select layer) + vulkan-freedreno-iceland
# + vulkan-swrast-iceland + vulkan-virtio-iceland + opencl-mesa-iceland, each with provides / conflicts of Arch's names
# (mesa, mesa-libgl, libgl, libegl, libgles, opengl-driver, libva-mesa-driver, vulkan-driver, vulkan-freedreno,
# vulkan-swrast, vulkan-virtio, vulkan-mesa-implicit-layers, opencl-mesa, opencl-driver).
pkgbase=mesa-iceland
_rusticl=true
pkgname=(
  mesa-iceland
  vulkan-freedreno-iceland
  vulkan-swrast-iceland
  vulkan-virtio-iceland
)
[[ $_rusticl == true ]] && pkgname+=(opencl-mesa-iceland)
